[{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2619250121","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/102090#issuecomment-2619250121","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/102090","id":2619250121,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6cHpXJ","user":{"login":"AThousandShips","id":96648715,"node_id":"U_kgDOBcK-Cw","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/96648715?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips","html_url":"https://github.com/AThousandShips","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-01-28T14:59:39Z","updated_at":"2025-01-28T15:04:40Z","body":"Try to avoid pushing so often for CI, you've run 21 times in CI in just 24 hours (and actually 20 in the last 11) and it risks cluttering the cache and taking up CI time","author_association":"MEMBER","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2619250121/reactions","total_count":2,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":2},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2622672945","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/102090#issuecomment-2622672945","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/102090","id":2622672945,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6cUtAx","user":{"login":"kleonc","id":9283098,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjkyODMwOTg=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/9283098?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/kleonc","html_url":"https://github.com/kleonc","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kleonc/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kleonc/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kleonc/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kleonc/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kleonc/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kleonc/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kleonc/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kleonc/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kleonc/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-01-29T19:38:50Z","updated_at":"2025-01-29T19:38:50Z","body":"> Some users want to have a method to calculate a path for the whole grid for many units, rather than one path for a single unit.\r\n\r\nCan confirm, seen e.g. usage of https://github.com/D2klaas/Godot-4-VectorFieldNavigation for 2D isometric grid (the grid logic was non-isometric though). Note this particular addon supports multiple targets for the flow map (in the mentioned usage I saw only one target being used though (the player)). So I'd say a proposal should be opened first, so it could be properly determined what's actually wanted/needed by the users.\r\n\r\n> Weight scale cannot be used to calculate a flow field,\r\n\r\nWhy though? I don't see a reason why this would be the case. I'd argue that flow map should give the same results[^1] as if you'd separately fetch path from each point (and doing so already uses/supports weight scale).\r\n\r\n[^1]: I guess discrepancies between equal cost paths might be potentially acceptable, so e.g. for going around a square shaped obstacle the flow map leading by its left+top edges but single path leading by its bottom+right edges would be fine (assuming equal costs).\r\n\r\n---\r\n\r\nAfter a brief search I haven't found an existing proposal for a flow map specifically, but there's #64326.\r\nAlso slightly related: https://github.com/godotengine/godot-proposals/issues/334.\r\n","author_association":"MEMBER","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2622672945/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2646617077","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/102090#issuecomment-2646617077","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/102090","id":2646617077,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6dwCv1","user":{"login":"realkotob","id":43449832,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQzNDQ5ODMy","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/43449832?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/realkotob","html_url":"https://github.com/realkotob","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/realkotob/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/realkotob/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/realkotob/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/realkotob/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/realkotob/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/realkotob/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/realkotob/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/realkotob/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/realkotob/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-02-09T21:53:06Z","updated_at":"2025-02-10T11:41:40Z","body":"Great work! Is it possible to set multiple goal tiles, or set a negative direction for the map (away from the goal)?\r\n\r\nThis would allow a loot more versatility and open up most of the common applications described here:\r\nhttps://www.roguebasin.com/index.php/The_Incredible_Power_of_Dijkstra_Maps\r\n\r\nhttps://www.roguebasin.com/index.php?title=Dijkstra_Maps_Visualized","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2646617077/reactions","total_count":2,"+1":2,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null}]